+
+**Verdict: REDESIGN. NO_NEW_MECHANISM for an unrestricted JC2 obstruction.** The strongest surviving computational mechanism is source-respecting constant-pivot elimination of the finite C block. It merits a circuit test, not a solver-performance promotion. The K16 rational-to-polynomial lemma is a substantive boundary result, but supplies no polynomial nonexistence theorem. JC2, full-family properness, source-to-stage8 necessity, and all-degree exclusion remain OPEN.
