+
+Opus also identifies a positive-row kernel with `J(P,G)=0`, although it permits `J(P,G)=constant`. Even a valid uniform rank floor 188 plus two rank-191 samples would not imply rank191 everywhere, global uniqueness, or a low-degree eliminated residual. Its “milliseconds over Q” oracle is unmeasured. Fable's exact rank-drop/decomposability converse lacks membership of the primitive generator in the actual C-space, and its enlarged block additionally contains h. These blind proofs remain defective after the later theorem. [Opus](/tmp/jc2-lane.mprOtd/inputs/ideation-20260906T1030Z-opus5.md:159), [Fable](/tmp/jc2-lane.mprOtd/inputs/ideation-20260906T1030Z-fable5.md:180).
+
+Same-source T2/T3 inclusion, after the explicit h/inverse graph maps, proves neither strict containment nor computational dominance. A larger locus can be harder to exclude. Fable's source grading also lacks an action: the fixed coefficient h3(4,5)=−8/3 has positive defect4, while h has fixed X coefficient1. Its inverse-row fallback survives; J0=1 and six affine gauge slices require actual source-preserving maps.
+
