+
+**Independent attack on the transverse theorem.** Accept its mathematical argument conditionally on the literal source/support assertions, at PRODUCER-CHECKED scope. With `X=x,W=y−x`, det=1, work over a characteristic-zero field. The reported restrictions are h(X,0)=X+c, G(X,0) monic quadratic, degG=66, Gtop=H⁶, H=(X+W)³W⁸, and degC≤35 with W-degree≤32. The unrestricted h-lift must preserve the fixed X term and top; this is a source/code obligation, not a name match.
+
+For nonconstant P∈V_C with J(P,G)=0, the charged common-polynomial theorem gives G=φ(R), P=ψ(R). Restriction to W=0 forces degφ=1 or2. The first forces degP≥66. The second forces degR=33 and ψ linear; `αRtop²=H⁶` forces a nonzero W³³ coefficient, forbidden in P. Thus the **full** C-kernel consists of constants. Both source hypotheses matter: dropping the transverse restriction allows G=H⁶,P=H; dropping C support allows R=H³+X,G=R²,P=R. [Proof and controls](/tmp/jc2-lane.mprOtd/inputs/linear-c-transverse-rank-astra-20260906.md:72).
+
+This gives a concrete post-cutoff counterexample to Fable's converse: D=b=0 makes G=h² composite, while the full C-rank remains191 because h has the forbidden W³³ term. The enlarged (C,a) block does have the commuting direction Δa=2,ΔC=0 there.
+
+Positive rows require a separate argument. The control J(X,X²+W)=1 distinguishes the maps without purporting to inhabit this source. At an actual Keller pair F,G, if P=ΔC+(Δa/2)h and J(P,G)=κ, then Q=P−(κ/j)F commutes with G. Keller forces G primitive and its centralizer k[G]. If κ≠0, degQ=99, impossible in k[G] of degree66; hence κ=0. Degree and W³³ support then force Δa=0 and ΔC constant. This is conditional uniqueness, not existence or uniform enlarged-block rank.
+
+Nonreduced base changes need more than fiberwise language. Over the polynomial Q-base, full rank191 at every geometric point makes the maximal-minor ideal unit. A Bezout combination of minors and adjugates gives a polynomial left inverse, which survives arbitrary base change. It supplies no chosen constant191 minor or cheap inverse. Conversely, the highest-face divisibility parametrization is only reduced: `D34=εX⁹W²⁵,C35=0` over Q[ε]/(ε²) satisfies its square equation without the claimed divisibility. Do not substitute that parametrization for the original scheme.
+
